{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":388430,"duration_api_ms":386953,"num_turns":22,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"149f2c5c-56ba-4674-943b-503395a25def","total_cost_usd":1.4570275000000001,"usage":{"input_tokens":4005,"cache_creation_input_tokens":87770,"cache_read_input_tokens":849530,"output_tokens":18547,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":87770,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":4005,"outputTokens":18547,"cacheReadInputTokens":849530,"cacheCreationInputTokens":87770,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.4570275000000001,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"amendments":[{"body":"In `AnimalState::add_reserve_by_feeding_units()` (biology.rs:491), the adult weight is computed as `f64::from(self.adult.count)` without multiplying by `ADULT_FEEDING_WEIGHT`, while `feeding_units()` (biology.rs:451) explicitly uses `ADULT_FEEDING_WEIGHT`. Both are numerically identical since the constant is 1.0, but they would silently diverge if the constant were ever changed. Use `f64::from(self.adult.count) * ADULT_FEEDING_WEIGHT` for consistency with the feeding_units() method that this function is documented to mirror.","rationale":"The doc comment says \"using the same weights that the legacy feeding model used for daily food demand,\" yet the code omits the ADULT_FEEDING_WEIGHT constant for one stage while using the named constants for the other two. This creates a latent maintenance trap where changing the constant would introduce a silent accounting inconsistency between food demand and reserve distribution."}],"summary":"Thorough review of the stage-structured shrimp population changes across 12 files. The implementation is well-structured: the stochastic-to-deterministic transfer conversion is mathematically sound with correct signed carry semantics; count conservation holds through spawning, hatch resolution, maturation, and mortality; stage transitions properly coordinate reserve transfers and maturation accumulators; the molt cycle refactoring cleanly separates timer-based readiness from multi-factor success scoring; TUI layout constraints are correctly adjusted for the new TDS scope annotation lines; and the snapshot/harness correctly include sub-adults in total population counts (fixing a prior omission). GH constants are properly derived from molar masses, replacing the old magic numbers with negligible precision change. All 16 shrimp population tests plus the full suite pass. One minor maintainability issue found: add_reserve_by_feeding_units omits ADULT_FEEDING_WEIGHT for the adult term while using named constants for sub-adult and juvenile, creating a latent inconsistency if the constant were ever changed."},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"f0ea6fd6-76ff-4791-aa9b-097f2e983ea5"}
